# Copy to deploy/.env on the VPS; never commit the real file.
VANA_DOMAIN=forest.example.com
# Generate URL-safe hex with: openssl rand -hex 32
VANA_DB_PASSWORD=replace_with_a_random_64_character_hex_value
# Changing this after first boot will NOT reset an existing world's seed.
VANA_WORLD_SEED=1

# AI agents living as animals (docs/2026-09-26-live-agents-design.md). Off unless 1. The
# live-agents world runs in real time; place drops also need the reward settings below.
# VANA_LIVE_AGENTS=1
# WORLD_HOURS_PER_REAL_HOUR=1
# VANA_AGENT_SLOTS=500
# VANA_AGENT_REGISTRATIONS_PER_NETWORK=5
# VANA_LIVE_SECRET=<openssl rand -hex 32>

# Optional observer insights from TypeSafe AI's Jev: a followed animal's likely next hour and
# highlights above "Happening now". Estimates only; the simulation never reads them. Off
# without a key. One call per followed animal per checkpoint plus one for highlights, capped
# per day (default 1000). The model defaults to jev-latest.
# TYPESAFE_AI_API_KEY=<your TypeSafe key>
# TYPESAFE_DAILY_CALLS=1000
# TYPESAFE_MODEL=jev-latest

# Observer rewards stay off unless all three are set (see deploy/README.md).
# VANA_REWARD_NETWORK=base
# VANA_REWARD_POLICY=first_valid
# VANA_REWARD_ADMIN_TOKEN=<openssl rand -hex 32>
# Anti-abuse, with their defaults: seconds an observer must watch before claiming, and
# winning claims allowed per wallet in any 24 hours.
# VANA_REWARD_MIN_WATCH_SECONDS=60
# VANA_REWARD_WALLET_DAILY_LIMIT=5
# Optional cap per visitor network address in 24 hours. Off by default: mobile carriers put
# many people behind one address, so a low number would lock out a whole area.
# VANA_REWARD_CLIENT_DAILY_LIMIT=50

# General per-visitor limits, with their defaults. A "visitor network" is one IPv4 address or one
# IPv6 /64, as seen through Caddy (VANA_TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS). An observer page makes well under one
# read a second and holds one /live connection, so normal visitors never meet these; a carrier or
# office NAT can put dozens of people behind one address, which is why they are high. 0 turns one off.
# Public read requests (world, animals, history, agents list...) per visitor network per minute,
# with bursts of a quarter of that. Health, rewards, admin and signed agent calls have
# their own limits and are not counted here. Past it: 429 with Retry-After.
# VANA_PUBLIC_READS_PER_MINUTE=1200
# Concurrent /live WebSocket connections in total, and from one visitor network. Past either, a
# new connection is closed with code 1013 ("try again later"); the observer waits 8-120 s with
# jitter before trying again. The total is the highest load tested on the reference machine,
# which held with little headroom (docs/2026-10-05-load-test.md); raise it only after a load
# test on the real host.
# VANA_LIVE_MAX_CONNECTIONS=1000
# VANA_LIVE_MAX_CONNECTIONS_PER_NETWORK=100
# New /live connections one visitor network may open per minute, in bursts of a quarter (each is
# sent the whole scene); 0 turns it off.
# VANA_LIVE_CONNECTS_PER_MINUTE=120

# Where the admin routes (/admin/…, /congo/admin/…) may be reached from: addresses and CIDR ranges,
# comma-separated, IPv4 or IPv6, as the API sees the visitor (behind Caddy and Cloudflare, the real
# address). Elsewhere they answer 404 before their token is read. Unset: from anywhere, by token.
# VANA_ADMIN_ALLOW_IPS=203.0.113.7,2001:db8::/48

# Operator metrics (Prometheus text) on the server's own internal port, never through Caddy; see
# "Metrics" in deploy/README.md. 127.0.0.1 keeps them inside the server container; 0.0.0.0 lets a
# scraper on the compose network reach server:9464. 0 turns them off.
# VANA_METRICS_PORT=9464
# VANA_METRICS_HOST=127.0.0.1
